PHP script is saving session state in the file system in an insecure way.  
It is intended to write out the username and whether or not the username is 
logged in.  Unfortunately, when it reads the session data from the file, it 
reads multiple lines as an array when really there should only be one line.  
Coupled with a write routine that allows you to store multiple lines (if 
you embed \n in the username), you can get an "admin 1" into the second
line of the session file.


